  LevelId: level_01_colonial
  DisplayName: Colonial Frontier (1675)
  HistoricalPeriod: "King Philip's War (1675\u20131676)"
  DateRange: "1675\u20131676"
  Location: New England Woodland Settlement
  ShortBriefing: Defend the colonial settlement outskirts amidst dense New England
    woodland and timber palisades.
  ObjectiveText: Survive the enemy waves and defend the settlement outskirts
  ControlHelp: 'Trigger: fire  |  Grip: reload  |  Take cover behind palisades'
  HistoricalNotes: King Philip's War (1675-1676) was fought between English colonists
    and the Wampanoag-led coalition. The Wampanoag people, led by Metacom (called
    King Philip by colonists), resisted colonial expansion. Both sides suffered devastating
    losses. This is depicted as a defensive skirmish only.
  SourceNotes: Lepore, Jill. "The Name of War" (1998). Schultz & Tougias, "King Philip's
    War" (1999).
